.Dd September 12, 2026
.Dt SNTP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sntp
.Nd set the clock from an NTP server, once
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Ar host
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends one SNTP request (RFC 4330) to
.Ar host
on UDP port 123 and sets the system clock to the transmit timestamp of
the reply, stepping it.
There is no slewing: on a machine without a battery clock the offset at
boot is measured in years.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p
Print the time the server gave, do not set the clock.
.It Fl t Ar seconds
Wait this long for an answer from each address of
.Ar host
(default 5).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr rdate 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written for MEECHO on the BIGTREETECH CB2, which has no clock the
system can read;
.Xr rdate 8
in this tree speaks only the RFC 868 time protocol, which public servers
no longer answer.
